(4638475, 668800, 86447, '<td valign="top">Water falls from the sky.   It then either goes down in the ground, getting filtered along the way, gets pumped back up for us to use again, or gets evaporated back up into the sky to start the cycle again.  We have the same amount of water that we''ve always had... it''s just recycled and refreshed continuously.<br/>All of that said, this is a wonderful image and quite deserves the 10 I''ve given to it.</td>', 'Water falls from the sky.   It then either goes down in the ground, getting filtered along the way, gets pumped back up for us to use again, or gets evaporated back up into the sky to start the cycle again.  We have the same amount of water that we''ve always had... it''s just recycled and refreshed continuously.All of that said, this is a wonderful image and quite deserves the 10 I''ve given to it.', '2008-04-14 11:42:41.000000', NULL, 1),
