(4651025, 668925, 39850, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Imagineer:</b></div><hr/><i> Striking abstract - like it. <br/> <br/>Some colour noise present which can be reduced by converting to LAB colour in PS and blurring channels ''a'' and/or ''b''. (Plenty of alternative methods too.) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you very much for this helpful comment.  Would like to hear the alternative methods, especially ones not using PS.  The noise (&amp;/or grain?) is usually a result of too tight a crop or a boost in saturation and something I always notice and dislike.<br/> <br/>-------------------------------------------------------<br/> <br/>Thanks to everyone else too for the comments, glad many of you liked this and ''saw'' what I was trying to ''show''.</td>', 'Originally posted by Imagineer: Striking abstract - like it.  Some colour noise present which can be reduced by converting to LAB colour in PS and blurring channels ''a'' and/or ''b''. (Plenty of alternative methods too.)   Thank you very much for this helpful comment.  Would like to hear the alternative methods, especially ones not using PS.  The noise (&/or grain?) is usually a result of too tight a crop or a boost in saturation and something I always notice and dislike. ------------------------------------------------------- Thanks to everyone else too for the comments, glad many of you liked this and ''saw'' what I was trying to ''show''.', '2008-04-21 06:16:53.000000', NULL, 0),
