(4651143, 668521, 30049, '<td valign="top">In the FWIW column...this was one of my top picks (gave it a 9).  I really enjoyed this for the creative take on the challenge theme and the calming abstract quality of it.  After seeing your notes, I wonder - why the ISO 1600 selection?  Was that to get the higher shutter speed of 1/1000, or an auto setting based on what your camera liked?  I ask only because the image did end up a little grainy which may have hurt the overall score somewhat.<br/> <br/>Anyway...Thanks for the refreshing POV.  Overall, nicely done.  :-)</td>', 'In the FWIW column...this was one of my top picks (gave it a 9).  I really enjoyed this for the creative take on the challenge theme and the calming abstract quality of it.  After seeing your notes, I wonder - why the ISO 1600 selection?  Was that to get the higher shutter speed of 1/1000, or an auto setting based on what your camera liked?  I ask only because the image did end up a little grainy which may have hurt the overall score somewhat. Anyway...Thanks for the refreshing POV.  Overall, nicely done.  :-)', '2008-04-21 09:06:32.000000', NULL, 0),
