(4651234, 668925, 50695, '<td valign="top">Like a Disco Heaven where you can''t stop the music.</td>', 'Like a Disco Heaven where you can''t stop the music.', '2008-04-21 09:46:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4651252, 668196, 68035, '<td valign="top">Bice shot and I love the sharpness and the integrity of the water drops in the illuminated central part of the leaves<br/> <br/>Great greens and a wonderful velvety textured feel to the leaf itself.  I was just wondering (if it had been possible) what this might have looked like with a square crop just tight around the water drops at the centre (although given your score I guess it did OK as it was!!!)</td>', 'Bice shot and I love the sharpness and the integrity of the water drops in the illuminated central part of the leaves Great greens and a wonderful velvety textured feel to the leaf itself.  I was just wondering (if it had been possible) what this might have looked like with a square crop just tight around the water drops at the centre (although given your score I guess it did OK as it was!!!)', '2008-04-21 09:53:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4651264, 669080, 12253, '<td valign="top">Very cool abstract!  Adding to favs!<br/></td>', 'Very cool abstract!  Adding to favs!', '2008-04-21 10:05:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4651275, 669078, 68035, '<td valign="top">Ron<br/> <br/>Nice shot to complete a hat-trick of 6''s on the bounce.  Fantastic job in terms of not only capturing the reflection so strongly but also on the strength and the integrity of the skyline given all the ambient illumination<br/> <br/>Good stuff!!!!</td>', 'Ron Nice shot to complete a hat-trick of 6''s on the bounce.  Fantastic job in terms of not only capturing the reflection so strongly but also on the strength and the integrity of the skyline given all the ambient illumination Good stuff!!!!', '2008-04-21 10:11:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4651280, 667660, 58691, '<td valign="top">Dave<br/>Congrats on the 6+ and top 50 finish. I do think the shorter exposure was good call on this one - providing solid blacks on the top and bottom. Good job. <br/></td>', 'DaveCongrats on the 6+ and top 50 finish. I do think the shorter exposure was good call on this one - providing solid blacks on the top and bottom. Good job. ', '2008-04-21 10:20:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4651299, 668196, 67579, '<td valign="top">Sweet photo girl :) the low angle lighting IMO really kicks this one up :)<br/> <br/>-dave</td>', 'Sweet photo girl :) the low angle lighting IMO really kicks this one up :) -dave', '2008-04-21 10:36:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4651343, 668800, 80831, '<td valign="top">Absolutely stunning on how this came out. The clarity of the tulip in the droplet and the droplet itself are amazing! This was my favorite entry of all of them. Beautiful work!</td>', 'Absolutely stunning on how this came out. The clarity of the tulip in the droplet and the droplet itself are amazing! This was my favorite entry of all of them. Beautiful work!', '2008-04-21 10:50:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4651361, 668988, 4793, '<td valign="top">Beautiful, congratulations</td>', 'Beautiful, congratulations', '2008-04-21 10:57:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4651362, 669018, 68947, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> Just read your comments...you really shouldn''t be such an optimist!  :-D  Looks like it did pretty well for you overall.  One thing that probably dinged the score on this (was mentioned in several comments) was the lemon.  Looking at the shot overall it appears to me that an overly healthy dose of NI (or some other noise reduction tool) was applied.  Yes, no?<br/> <br/>Anyway.  Congrats on a new image in your PB lineup.  :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ahhhhh........Barry, my optimism stems from feeling like I''ve been knocking myself over the head with a sledgehammer in challenges lately! The ones that I felt would do really well, have bombed horribly and been very disappointing, getting cut up in the comments, so I figured I may as well expect the same score with this one as well! *grin*  It''s easier to fall from one stair height in expectation, then 10! :)  Thank you for your boost in comments!  It''s well appreciated!</td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: Just read your comments...you really shouldn''t be such an optimist!  :-D  Looks like it did pretty well for you overall.  One thing that probably dinged the score on this (was mentioned in several comments) was the lemon.  Looking at the shot overall it appears to me that an overly healthy dose of NI (or some other noise reduction tool) was applied.  Yes, no? Anyway.  Congrats on a new image in your PB lineup.  :-)   Ahhhhh........Barry, my optimism stems from feeling like I''ve been knocking myself over the head with a sledgehammer in challenges lately! The ones that I felt would do really well, have bombed horribly and been very disappointing, getting cut up in the comments, so I figured I may as well expect the same score with this one as well! *grin*  It''s easier to fall from one stair height in expectation, then 10! :)  Thank you for your boost in comments!  It''s well appreciated!', '2008-04-21 10:57:58.000000', NULL, 0);
