(4658822, 668686, 81535, '<td valign="top">I like what you did with the original photograph. Not a new idea, yet a very artistic result displaying your creative mind.</td>', 'I like what you did with the original photograph. Not a new idea, yet a very artistic result displaying your creative mind.', '2008-04-25 10:37:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4659474, 668848, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I really like this shot.  I am a sucker for negative space, and I like how everything is on one side of the frame.  You can almost feel the fish breaking for the open water there. <br/> <br/>Technically, it has the feeling of an underexposed shot that was corrected in pp thereby leaving it with some edginess or graininess.  At first glance, I didn''t like that.  This, I think, is a shot that would have to grow on you, because the more I look at it, the more I think it would work. <br/> <br/>It has that "advant-garde" feeling that says, "I wouldn''t put it on my wall, but I might put it in a fine art magazine."  <br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, I really like this shot.  I am a sucker for negative space, and I like how everything is on one side of the frame.  You can almost feel the fish breaking for the open water there.  Technically, it has the feeling of an underexposed shot that was corrected in pp thereby leaving it with some edginess or graininess.  At first glance, I didn''t like that.  This, I think, is a shot that would have to grow on you, because the more I look at it, the more I think it would work.  It has that "advant-garde" feeling that says, "I wouldn''t put it on my wall, but I might put it in a fine art magazine."   Karma', '2008-04-25 17:39:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4659490, 669113, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I love this shot.  It is "anchored" (no pun intended) strongly in the lower right hand side with the smattering of boats on the left providing a neat contrast and adding balance.  It does *feel* tilted to the right to me, though I don''t think it is.  I suspect it is more of an illusion created by the boats and the clouds.<br/> <br/>I really like the bw conversion and how you have captured a lot of detail without making it busy.<br/> <br/>It has a very dark ominous feeling.  You can almost feel the storm blowing in. . .<br/> <br/>Great work</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, I love this shot.  It is "anchored" (no pun intended) strongly in the lower right hand side with the smattering of boats on the left providing a neat contrast and adding balance.  It does *feel* tilted to the right to me, though I don''t think it is.  I suspect it is more of an illusion created by the boats and the clouds. I really like the bw conversion and how you have captured a lot of detail without making it busy. It has a very dark ominous feeling.  You can almost feel the storm blowing in. . . Great work', '2008-04-25 17:52:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4660021, 668786, 87278, '<td valign="top">Congrats! I kinda begun to recognize your work even though i ''m no photographer. I saw this photograph guessed it cd be yours and checked the name to confirm!</td>', 'Congrats! I kinda begun to recognize your work even though i ''m no photographer. I saw this photograph guessed it cd be yours and checked the name to confirm!', '2008-04-26 06:21:39.000000', NULL, 0),
